# SOLVENT_DATABASE_URL is the LIVE indexer database (the backfill daemon's).
SOLVENT_DATABASE_URL=postgres://solvent:solvent@localhost:5432/solvent?sslmode=disable
SOLVENT_RPC_OP=https://mainnet.optimism.io
SOLVENT_RPC_ETH=https://eth.llamarpc.com
SOLVENT_POLL_INTERVAL=5s
# Collateral snapshot sweep cadence (default 1h) and price poll cadence
# (default 1m); Go duration strings, must be positive.
#SOLVENT_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL=1h
#SOLVENT_PRICE_INTERVAL=1m
# Health/readiness endpoint bind address (default 127.0.0.1:9090; "off"
# disables the listener).
#SOLVENT_HEALTH_ADDR=127.0.0.1:9090
# TEST_DATABASE_URL points at the SCRATCH database solvent_test — NEVER at
# `solvent`: the store test suite Migrate+TRUNCATEs twelve tables including
# raw_logs, so aiming it at the live database destroys the backfill (Task 9
# wave 10 DB split; `make db-up` provisions solvent_test idempotently, and
# cmd/reconcile refuses to run when both DSNs resolve to one database).
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://solvent:solvent@localhost:5432/solvent_test?sslmode=disable
# cmd/reconcile RPC overrides (fall back to SOLVENT_RPC_* when unset). The
# ETH recon endpoint must be ARCHIVE-STATE capable: the W1 golden row is a
# live pinned eth_call at block 25,584,990, which non-archive endpoints
# reject as pruned. Keys belong in your local .env only — never committed.
#SOLVENT_RECON_RPC_ETH=
#SOLVENT_RECON_RPC_OP=
# Read-only evidence tests (invariants_live_test.go) gate on this — point it
# at the live database for the receipt run; the connection is forced
# read-only and never migrates.
#SOLVENT_RECON_DATABASE_URL=
# Path to Foundry's anvil binary (not on PATH) — opts in the fork-replay test (internal/forkreplay); unset = skip.
#ANVIL_BIN=
# Archive-capable OP RPC URL anvil forks from (the dRPC OP endpoint works) — unset = the fork-replay test skips.
#ANVIL_FORK_RPC=
# Archive-capable ETH MAINNET RPC URL anvil forks from — opts in the P3 Task 3
# pipeline-replay harness (internal/pipelinereplay, `make test-pipeline-replay`)
# together with ANVIL_BIN; unset = its legs skip. Deliberately SEPARATE from
# ANVIL_FORK_RPC above, which is the OP endpoint Task 10 forks.
#
# It must be ARCHIVE-COMPLETE: the legs fork ETH mainnet at blocks 20,714,020
# and 21,469,984, and anvil PROXIES every pre-fork eth_getLogs/eth_call to this
# upstream. A free-tier Alchemy key is the sanctioned choice here (probe A3's
# targeted carve-out: opt-in, on-demand, ~100 getLogs per full run) — the
# harness therefore walks at WINDOW 10, because the upstream's 10-block getLogs
# cap becomes the harness's cap. Never point bulk backfill traffic at this key.
#ANVIL_FORK_RPC_ETH=
